==========================================================================================
[5-STATE FPGA CONFIG & OPTICAL AVDD HARDWARE INTERLOCK VERIFICATION (ON TOP OF bb87623)]
==========================================================================================
- Fixed `bb87623` blind RC timer vulnerability (where `AVDD_OPT_BIAS` would turn ON even when FPGA configuration failed with `CDONE=0` or during MCU reset, and stayed ON for >16ms after `1V8_OPT_VDD` power-down).
- Implemented 5-State Schottky Peak-Hold + Dual-Clamp Interlock (`Ball D3 CDONE/VSYNC` -> `D1 (RB521S-30) + R_CHG=10R` -> `C_HOLD=22nF || R_BLEED=2.2M`, with `D_RST` to `FPGA_CRESET_B` [10k PD] and `D_VDD` to `1V8_OPT_VDD`):
    * State 1 (POR / MCU Reset, `CRESET_B=0.00V`): `V_EN = 0.000V <= 0.40V (VIL)` -> OFF (`0.00V`, 120R discharge).
    * State 2 (Config In Progress or Config Failure, `CRESET_B=1.80V, CDONE=0.00V`): `V_EN = 0.000V <= 0.40V (VIL)` -> OFF permanently.
    * State 3 (Config Success + 60.000Hz `1.000us` VSYNC): `tau_chg = 0.77us`, `V_1st = 1.148V`, `V_peak = 1.580V`, `V_valley = 1.120V >= 0.95V (VIH)` (+170mV margin) -> ON continuously.
    * State 4 (VSYNC Loss / FPGA Freeze Watchdog): `t_wdog_off = 66.5ms` (< 100ms) -> OFF automatically.
    * State 5 (Reset or `1V8_OPT_VDD` Power-Down): `D_RST` / `D_VDD` fast clamp `t_fast_off = 2.31us` (<= 5.0us) -> OFF before `1V8_OPT_VDD` decays.
- `21/21` Negative Fault Injections (CHK-08): 100% CAUGHT -> PASS.
